# DEPTH JUMP

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Depth Jump is an advanced plyometric exercise performed by stepping from an elevated platform, absorbing landing forces and immediately rebounding into a maximal vertical jump.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the most effective exercises for developing reactive strength and stretch-shortening cycle efficiency.

---

# Philosophy

The goal is not to jump high.

The goal is to minimize ground contact time while maximizing force production.

CAS selects the Depth Jump only for athletes who possess sufficient strength, landing mechanics and tissue resilience.

